"""Consolidate device-only checks without fabricating manual passes."""
HUMAN_CASES = [
 dict(id='human-screen-v4',title='1. Optional: tell me if anything feels wrong on your screen',need='Your tablet. No USB or computer.',why='Code checks cannot judge your eyesight, comfort or spoken screen-reader experience.',steps=['I checked Home, Learn, English/Arabic layout, search and the dark format picker on your actual tablet. You do not need to repeat those checks. Only use the app normally and note anything uncomfortable or confusing. On Home open a group, pin/unpin a tool, and search. On Learn search for a question and open it.','Open Format USB and its filesystem list WITHOUT connecting a USB or starting Format. Check that names, selected options and custom-size fields are readable.','Switch English/Arabic and rotate once. If you use large text or TalkBack, try your normal settings.','Only report clipping, unreadable colours, confusing wording, missed taps or anything that feels wrong. You do not need to repeat every tool.'],expected='You can read and use the main screens comfortably. Note the screen/tool and language if something is wrong.'),
 dict(id='human-usb-read-v4',title='2. Connect a real USB and try the read tools',need='A spare USB, OTG adapter, and a backup of its contents.',why='The automated checks use simulated disks; they cannot reproduce your USB controller, cable or power supply.',steps=['Connect the spare. Open Select a USB. Deny permission once, then select again and allow it. Check the displayed model and capacity identify this spare.','Run Full USB analyzer, Sector viewer, Read benchmark, Random read benchmark and Read surface scan, one after another. These are read tools.','If the drive contains supported NTFS/ext files, try Browse USB files and export one known file to internal Downloads. Open that file and compare it with the original.','For a long scan, go Back, leave the app, lock/unlock, and return. Cancel the scan if you want; make sure it says cancelled rather than successful.','Write the USB model/capacity and the name of any tool that failed. Do not unplug during a write or use personal data for failure testing.'],expected='Correct USB identity; read tools finish or give an accurate error; returning to the app shows the same job. Existing USB files remain intact.'),
 dict(id='human-usb-write-v4',title='3. Try real USB writes on an EMPTY spare',need='An EMPTY labelled spare that may be erased. A second empty spare only if testing Clone USB.',why='Real permission, USB disconnect, power and physical readback cannot be proved by files in tablet storage.',steps=['Confirm this is the EMPTY spare. In Format USB choose a supported format appropriate for the drive, then cancel the confirmation once. Nothing should start. Repeat and confirm only for this spare.','For the write tools you will publish: write a known supplied raw test image then Verify an image; Backup that spare, restore the backup to the same spare and verify; run Zero-fill followed by Verify zero-filled; run Full capacity test. Each operation erases/replaces data, so keep using only the EMPTY spare.','If you have two empty spares, also try Clone USB and verify the copy. If not, write Clone not tested — need second spare.','For partition names/active flag, MBR/GPT conversion, filesystem check or Read-error map: ask me for a focused follow-up for your actual USB layout. Do not guess technical options or intentionally damage a drive.','During one long write go Back and return; check it stays one job. Cancel another write early, wait for it to stop, and check Activity says cancelled/incomplete. Do not deliberately pull power.','In notes list each tool you tried as worked / failed / not tried, and copy any exact error. Physical power-loss/controller tests remain specialist work; do not mark them passed here.'],expected='Only the chosen spare changes; independent readback/Verify agrees; cancellation and background progress are honest. Untested write tools stay explicitly listed in notes.'),
 dict(id='human-provider-v4',title='4. Check Android file-picker permissions once',need='The small ZIP pack in Downloads; optionally the cloud/removable provider you actually plan to use.',why='Synthetic archive/engine tests cannot exercise another Android app’s document provider or its access grants.',steps=['In Create ZIP choose two files from the small pack; use Add files to add another. Save into a new internal Downloads folder. Extract the ZIP, open the extracted text files in Android Files and check their names/content.','In Browse & export WIM files choose the supplied sample WIM, list it, tap a listed path and export it. In WIM folder export use / for the whole sample and open an exported text file.','Cancel a source picker and a destination picker once. Reopen the app with the USB disconnected: no unsolicited folder error should appear.','Only if you use a cloud/removable provider, repeat a small ZIP create/extract there. A provider that cannot support an operation must show a clear error and leave originals intact.','Record the provider name and any failing tool. Engine round trips and malformed-input testing are already assigned to the developer; do not repeat them.'],expected='Actual Android file selection, staged ZIP inputs, named folders and WIM export work; cancelling does not start a job; Home does not show the old unsolicited error.'),
 dict(id='human-mount-v4',title='5. Computer check: can the formatted USB really store files?',need='A compatible computer and an EMPTY spare. If unavailable choose Blocked and say which computer is missing.',why='An app reporting Format complete does not prove Windows/Linux/macOS can mount its filesystem.',steps=['Only test filesystems you intend to advertise and for which you have a compatible computer. Use the EMPTY spare, Format USB, Automatic allocation and the supported MBR/GPT option.','Windows/Linux: FAT32, exFAT, NTFS. Linux: ext2/ext3/ext4, Btrfs and XFS; F2FS requires a Linux setup that supports it. UDF needs an OS/tool that supports the app’s disk layout. macOS: HFS+ and APFS. The newer UDF/HFS+/APFS/Btrfs/XFS engines remain experimental, limited to 32 GiB and 512-byte sectors; APFS requires GPT.','After EACH format safely reconnect on the compatible computer. Copy a small file to the drive, open it, safely eject/reconnect, and open it again. Return it to the app and try its supported read/check tool.','Write one line per format/table: e.g. NTFS GPT — Windows 11 — copied/reopened OK. Also list formats not checked; one successful format does not pass all formats.','FAT12 needs only 2–32 MiB and FAT16 8 MiB–2 GiB test media/images. Their size refusals are expected; do not buy unusual USB hardware for them. ReFS/LUKS are unavailable and require no test.','Do not guess or mark the whole family Worked if only one format was checked. Choose Not sure for a partial session and keep the successful individual lines in notes.'],expected='Each tested format mounts on its intended OS and files survive reconnecting. Missing OS/filesystem evidence stays listed as blocked; unsupported features stay unavailable.'),
 dict(id='human-boot-v4',title='6. Computer check: boot and persistence (only with suitable equipment)',need='A spare USB, a computer you can boot from USB, and your own permitted Linux/Windows images or official Ventoy package. No images are supplied.',why='Generated test images cannot boot; real firmware, Secure Boot, operating-system installers and persistence require a computer.',steps=['If you have no bootable computer/images, select Blocked and write what is missing. Do not download anything solely to satisfy this checklist.','For raw image writing, use a supported hybrid Linux ISO, then Verify. Boot that spare using your computer’s boot menu. Record the Linux release and UEFI/BIOS/Secure Boot setting.','If claiming Windows UEFI preparation, prepare your own supported Windows ISO using that tool and reach the installer welcome screen. Stop before installing to any computer disk.','If claiming Ventoy install/GPT/update/library, import your official package, prepare only the spare, and boot the supported images you actually claim. Record package/version, table and firmware mode; check update keeps the existing image files.','If claiming Linux persistence, use a compatible distro/layout. Boot with persistence, create a harmless file in the live system, reboot again with persistence, and check the file remains.','Record separate results for raw boot, Windows UEFI, Ventoy MBR/GPT/update/library and persistence. Missing tests are still blocked; reaching a menu alone does not prove all images boot.'],expected='Each claimed boot path actually reaches its expected screen. Persistence survives reboot. No computer installation or changes to internal disks are needed.'),
 dict(id='human-console-v4',title='7. Console check (only if you have the consoles)',need='Your own compatible PS2/PS3 setup, exact loader/version and permitted source images. Otherwise choose Blocked.',why='Byte-perfect conversions and parts can be checked here; actual loader/game compatibility requires the target console.',steps=['I handle CSO/ZSO/CHD byte round trips and split/join hashes. You do not need to repeat those arithmetic/file tests.','For PS2 USBExtreme or ZSO, use your own permitted compatible source and the exact supported loader. Check the generated title/files appear and the intended content actually opens. Record the loader and version.','For PS3 raw split files, use the compatible manager/rejoin workflow your setup requires. Merely placing split parts on a drive does not make them directly playable.','For CHD or CSO consumer support, test only the emulator/loader/version you plan to claim; stored CHD creation is data-only and does not support CD track creation.','List separate tool/loader outcomes and missing equipment in notes. Do not buy consoles just for this test.'],expected='Only tested consumer/loader compatibility is claimed; missing consoles remain blocked, not failed file conversions.'),
 dict(id='human-other-devices-v4',title='8. Other devices and accessibility — send to a tester if needed',need='Other Android versions/ABIs, a person using TalkBack/keyboard, or a tester with that equipment.',why='This tablet cannot prove runtime behavior on Android 6, Intel devices, other USB controllers or another person’s accessibility setup.',steps=['Do not repeat the full tool checklist yourself. Share the same QA APK with a trusted tester who already has the missing device, if you choose to. No sharing is automatic.','Ask them to open Home/Learn, change language, use one custom picker, create/extract a small ZIP and run a read-only USB tool if they have an OTG spare. Record Android, WebView, ABI and model.','For TalkBack/keyboard, check names/selected states, focus inside the picker and Back returning to its trigger. Record any unreachable control.','Mark unavailable Android/ABI/accessibility environments Blocked in notes. Build/ABI audits are automated and are not a substitute for these runtime checks.','Power-loss, faulty USB controllers and special-provider laboratory tests stay with a specialist; ask me to prepare only the exact follow-up needed for your claimed release scope.'],expected='Actual tested environments and failures are documented. Untested environments remain explicit limitations rather than another long assignment for you.')
]
TOOL_SUITES = {
'hash':['test.sh','test_batch.sh'],'checksums':['test_batch.sh'],'zip':['test_archive.sh'],'extract':['test_archive.sh'],'createzip':['test_archive.sh','test_batch.sh'],'tar':['test_images.sh'],'archives':['test_archive.sh'],'split':['test_batch.sh'],'join':['test_batch.sh'],'compressedImage':['test_containers.sh'],'cso':['test_containers.sh'],'zso':['test_containers.sh'],'chd':['test_chd.sh'],'dmg':['test_dmg.sh'],'optical':['test_images.sh'],'imageinfo':['test_analyzer.sh'],'fatImage':['test_fat_images.sh'],'wimExplore':['test_wim.sh','test_wim_tree.sh'],'wimTree':['test_wim_tree.sh'],'wimSplit':['test_wim.sh'],'fileBenchmark':['test_bench.sh'],'info':['test_analyzer.sh'],'hex':['test.sh'],'benchmark':['test_bench.sh'],'randomread':['test_bench.sh'],'scan':['test.sh'],'readMap':['test_learning.sh'],'format':['test_native.sh','test.sh','test_f2fs.sh'],'write':['test.sh'],'verify':['test.sh'],'backup':['test.sh'],'clone':['test.sh'],'convertTable':['test.sh'],'partitionMeta':['test_analyzer.sh'],'filesystemCheck':['test_native.sh','test_fsimage.sh'],'fsUsb':['test_fsimage.sh'],'fsImage':['test_fsimage.sh'],'wipe':['test_batch.sh'],'verifyZero':['test_batch.sh'],'capacity':['test.sh'],'ventoyInstall':['test_images.sh'],'ventoyGpt':['test_images.sh'],'ventoyUpdate':['test_images.sh'],'ventoy':['test_images.sh'],'persistence':['test_native.sh'],'windows':['test_wim.sh','test_images.sh'],'consoleParts':['test_console_parts.sh'],'usbExtreme':['test_usbextreme.sh'],'diagnostic':['test_learning.sh'],'report':['test_learning.sh'],'planner':['test_learning.sh']}
def apply(sections,evidence):
 import json
 from pathlib import Path
 original_path=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/"artifacts/user-tests-2026-11-07.json"
 original=json.loads(original_path.read_text()) if original_path.exists() else {"cases":{}}
 worked={k for k,v in original["cases"].items() if v["status"]=="pass"}
 for g in sections:
  suites=TOOL_SUITES.get(g['id'][5:],[]) if g['id'].startswith('tool-') else []
  if g['id'].startswith('format-'):suites=['test_native.sh','test.sh','test_f2fs.sh']
  if g['id'] in ['startup','pickers','start-here-v2','changed-flows-v3']:suites=['test_learning.sh']
  g['developerOwned']=True
  for c in g['cases']:
   c['developerOwned']=True
   if c['id'] in worked:c['needsRetest']=False;c['skipUserWorked']=True
   c['automationSuites']=suites
   c['automationScope']='Developer owns this detailed case. Listed passing suites cover generated-fixture/code behavior only, not every instruction in this case. Physical/provider/visual/boot checks are consolidated into the five equipment sessions.'
 user=dict(id='human-only-v4',name='Only what needs your equipment or judgment — five equipment sessions + optional comfort',cases=[])
 for item in HUMAN_CASES:
  c=dict(item,guided=True,humanOnly=True,needsRetest=True)
  if c['id'] in ['human-usb-read-v4','human-usb-write-v4']:
   c['humanOnly']=False;c['developerOwned']=True;c['automationSuites']=[];c['automationScope']='Not assigned to you: read tools already Worked; remaining write algorithms and bounded physical command tests belong to the developer. Full-drive, long-duration and two-drive cases remain explicitly separate.'
  if c['id']=='human-screen-v4':c['optional']=True
  if c['id']=='human-provider-v4':
   c['title']='1. Only other Android storage providers you actually use'
   c['steps']=['Skip ZIP creation/extraction and other file workflows you already marked Worked. Do not repeat them.', 'Only if you plan to use a different cloud/removable provider, try a SMALL known-file read and output there. Use a new output folder; record provider name, tool and exact error.', 'If internal storage is your only intended provider and it already worked, mark Not applicable with that reason. No extra cloud account or purchase is needed.']
   c['expected']='Only additional provider compatibility is recorded. Your previous Worked results remain accepted; missing providers are not guessed.'
  if c['id']=='human-mount-v4':
   c['title']='2. Computer compatibility for an already formatted drive'
   c['steps']=['Do not repeat your successful format operations. This is a separate compatibility question: can a real computer mount the current filesystem?', 'If you have a compatible computer, connect the already formatted spare, copy a small file, safely eject/reconnect and reopen it. Record the current format, computer OS and result.', 'Windows usually needs FAT/exFAT/NTFS; Linux is needed for ext/Btrfs/XFS/F2FS; macOS is needed for HFS+/APFS. Do not reformat through every filesystem for this session.', 'If you lack the needed computer, choose Blocked and state which one. Other filesystem/OS combinations stay specialist compatibility work, without changing your original format passes.']
  if c['id']=='human-boot-v4':c['title']='3. Real computer boot and Linux persistence'
  if c['id']=='human-console-v4':c['title']='4. Real console or target emulator compatibility'
  if c['id']=='human-other-devices-v4':
   c['title']='5. Missing devices, second USB and accessibility equipment'
   c['steps'].append('A real two-drive clone needs a second empty spare. Do not repeat earlier read benchmarks/formatting just to finish this session. Record missing equipment instead.')
  user['cases'].append(c)
 sections.insert(0,user)
 return sections
